<h1>Real Estate</h1>
<p class="story-lead">A property team was running three towers from inboxes and a shared sheet. Requests, vendor visits, and the asset list never sat on the same building.</p>
<p>The handover between the day team and the evening team started with a phone call. A leak logged in the morning was still open at night because the vendor update lived in another thread.</p>
<p>They put work orders, inspections, and vendor visits on the building record. The evening team now opens the same request the day team raised, and a repeat fault shows the history instead of starting again.</p>
